(BAS-43 - the blank-line rule applies uniformly: `while`, `for each`,
 `repeat` and `on error` all terminate their body on a blank line,
 whatever the last body statement was. Each block below is closed only by
 its blank line, and `Print "end"` runs once at the top level.
